    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 28 tests, 0 failures/errors (including the new `Cp17Tests`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `locality` field is a derived value surfaced on `GET /api/owners/{id}` (and every other owner response). Three edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `locality` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it. Documented the derivation and the `UNKNOWN` fallback.\n\n2. **`.../rest/function/common/Localities.java`** (new) \u2014 the fixed city-to-region table and `region(city)` lookup: `Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`, else `\"UNKNOWN\"`.\n\n3. **`.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `locality` that calls `Localities.region(owner.getCity())`, mirroring how `displayName`, `initials`, and `membershipTier` are already derived at mapping time.\n\nDeriving it in the mapper (rather than persisting a new column) keeps `locality` always consistent with the stored `city` and requires no schema change or pipeline step. `Cp17Tests` confirms `Sydney \u2192 \"NSW\"` and an unlisted city \u2192 `\"UNKNOWN\"`.",
